       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16 g/day, which is about five times the maximum daily dose. At that level it is a toxic dose, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be appropriate. You also haven't given a rationale. Entering it could seriously harm the patient through GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, or CNS effects.\n\nHere are some other ways forward:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** Give me the dose and frequency, for example 800 mg PO three times daily, and I'll enter it now.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or clinical toxicology.** If you're trying to reach a particular therapeutic goal, they can help find a safe regimen.\n- **Enter it directly.** If you have a documented reason I'm not seeing, you can place the order yourself. Pharmacy verification would still be expected.\n\nWhat are you trying to treat? I can help work out an appropriate regimen."
